      "headline": "Info Edge Q2 billings rise 12.8%, recruitment up 12.6%",
      "essay": "Info Edge reported standalone billings of INR 8.22 billion (USD 63.4 million) for the September quarter, up 12.8% from INR 7.29 billion a year earlier. Recruitment solutions, the Naukri business, grew 12.6% to INR 6.14 billion. 99acres led with 21.2% growth to INR 1.48 billion, while Jeevansathi rose 18.4% to INR 397 million. Shiksha fell 27.2% to INR 205 million. For the first half, billings rose 13.5% to INR 15.59 billion.\n\nThe growth was slower than the 14.4% in Q1. Management said the recruitment figure was affected by one-off deferrals in renewals, with underlying growth at 14-15% after adjusting for timing. Kotak maintained its FY2027 billings growth expectation of 14-15%.\n\nThe update is subject to audit committee and board review. The stock fell 3.46% on 8 October before the update, then rose 4.4% on 9 October to an intraday high of INR 1,235.",
