      "headline": "Deeptech founders ask government to be first customer",
      "essay": "Deeptech startups are asking the government to act as an early customer to help them compete with global incumbents, founders said at a panel at ETSA 2026 titled 'Building the Hard Stuff in India'. Geopolitical tensions are also adding to supply chain issues for India's space sector.\n\nKshitij Khandelwal, cofounder and CTO of spacetech startup Pixxel, said tensions in West Asia have made it harder to source critical components, as demand for airborne sensors and related equipment has risen, driving up costs.\n\nDheemanth Nagaraj, cofounder and CEO of Agrani Labs, said Indian deeptech companies need the government to become an early customer and create markets for domestically developed technologies.\n\nWatch whether the government changes its procurement rules to buy from deeptech startups at an early stage.",
