    {
      "headline": "Bitcoin seen as best single crypto pick despite 35% drawdown",
      "essay": "Bitcoin is still down nearly 35% from its October 2025 all-time high of $126,000, and other cryptocurrencies are outperforming it, but one analyst argues Bitcoin remains the single best crypto to own. The case rests on track record: Bitcoin has traded since 2009, more than 17 years, and has never had back-to-back losing years. Its drawdowns have hit 65% or more, but good years have more than made up for bad ones, with frequent doubles.\n\nThe comparison is with newer tokens. Hyperliquid's HYPE is up more than 230% this year, but it only started trading in late 2024, so there isn't enough data to judge staying power. BlackRock has called Bitcoin a \"unique portfolio diversifier,\" and its history of being uncorrelated with major asset classes supports that. Bitcoin also remains the market bellwether: as Bitcoin goes, so goes the crypto market.\n\nFor a holder, this is the long-term bull case rather than a trading signal. The near-term price is weak, but the argument is that no other crypto has Bitcoin's cycle history or its role as the asset institutions treat as the category's core.",
